=============================================================================
=               Scales and Modes in Scottish Traditional Music              =
=                                  Jack Campin                              =
=============================================================================


The Ranges of Traditional Tunes
===============================

1. Vocal Ranges
===============

The dumbed-down "seven mode" system popularized in the folk scene assumes
that the same pattern of pitches is repeated in every octave.  In most of
the world's musical traditions, that isn't true.  

Most human music is made with voices or instruments of range much more
limited than those of the jazz group, rock band or classical orchestra.
The ordinary human voice has a range a bit over an octave.  The vocal
ranges defined by Western classical music use two octaves; only trained
singers can use the extremes of that, whatever their vocal type.  

